qarchiver (2.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix mojibake for archives whose member names are not UTF-8 (GBK/GB18030/
    Big5): the libarchive backend no longer decodes raw names with the process
    locale, and no longer passes hdrcharset (which fails outright on non-UTF-8
    locales).  Legacy encodings are now ranked by how plausible their common
    character blocks are, with the system locale only breaking near-ties, so
    Big5 archives are correct on every locale.
  * Fix Explorer compression entries always producing ZIP (command id is in
    lpVerb, not lpVerbW), restore menu icons and open the created archive.
  * Install a versioned QArchiverShell DLL so in-place upgrades survive an
    Explorer-locked shell extension; clean old copies during upgrade/uninstall.
  * Improve compression log output and the 7-Zip benchmark (thread selector,
    streamed output, progress heartbeat and result summary).
  * Open the archive created by the Explorer menu on the next event loop
    iteration instead of re-entering the archive manager from inside its own
    signal, and reveal only one window when compressing a multi-selection.

 -- shenmo <shenmo@spark-app.store>  Mon, 24 Nov 2026 21:40:00 +0800

